.Dd October 12, 2026
.Dt ARCANA-CONSOLE 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm arcana-console
.Nd the Arcana web console
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm service
.Cm arcana_console
.Cm start | stop | restart | status
.Pp
.Ev ARCANA_WEB_CONF Ns = Ns Pa web.conf
.Nm kore
.Op Fl d
.Fl c Pa kore.conf
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The arcana console is
.Xr kore 1
with the module
.Pa arcana-console.so :
it serves the web application and its JSON API, logs its one user in
with WebAuthn, keeps the list of hosts, and talks to the
.Xr arcana-agent 8
of each host over cblink, with mutual TLS over TCP or through a local
socket.
It runs unprivileged; everything that changes a host is done by that
host's
.Xr arcana-agent 8 .
.Pp
The console shows, per host: its jails with their state and actions;
its rc.d services with their
.Xr rc.conf 5
variables; the routing table, nexthops, connections and sockets; the
packages that can be upgraded, on the host and in running jails; and
CPU, memory and ZFS usage.
Every call to a host is listed with a trace of what the host did.
.Sh CONFIGURATION
Two files configure it.
.Pa kore.conf
is Kore's own: the address to bind (one
.Cm bind
line per address family), the RSA certificate for HTTPS, the user the
worker runs as, and an
.Cm include
of
.Pa routes.conf .
.Pa web.conf ,
named by the environment variable
.Ev ARCANA_WEB_CONF ,
is the console's, in UCL:
.Bl -tag -width "update_check"
.It Va rp_id
The WebAuthn relying party: the console's host name as the browser sees
it, or a parent domain of it.
Keys are bound to the
.Va rp_id
they were registered under: after changing it, enrol again.
Required.
.It Va origin
The exact origin the browser uses, such as
.Ql https://console.example .
Opened at any other address, or without HTTPS other than on localhost,
the browser refuses security keys with a
.Dq SecurityError
.Pq Do The operation is insecure Dc in Firefox ;
the login screen then says which address the console is set up for.
Required.
.It Va rp_name
The name security keys show.
Default
.Ql Arcana .
.It Va datadir
Where the registered keys, the server list, the setup token and, without
.Va tls ,
the console's own certificate authority are kept; mode 0700, owned by
the worker's user.
Default
.Pa /var/db/arcana .
.It Va cookie_secure
Whether the session cookie is marked Secure.
Default true.
.It Va tls
A block naming certificates for
.Xr arcana-agent 8
over TCP:
.Va ca ,
the authority that issued the hosts' certificates;
.Va cert
and
.Va key ,
the console's client certificate; and optionally
.Va ca_key ,
the authority's key, which lets the console enrol hosts.
Without the block the console makes an authority of its own in
.Va datadir
at first start and enrols hosts with it; see
.Xr arcana-enrol 8 .
.It Va update_check
False stops the console from asking the release feed for newer
versions.
Default true.
.It Va update_url
Another feed, in the shape of GitHub's
.Pa releases/latest .
.It Va agent_binary
The
.Xr arcana-agent 8
the console sends to hosts when asked to update them.
Default
.Pa /usr/local/sbin/arcana-agent ,
the one installed with the console.
.It Va agent_source
A git repository with the Arcana tree.
When set, a host can be asked to build
.Xr arcana-agent 8
from it; the console keeps what the host sends back in
.Pa agent/
under
.Va datadir
and sends that instead of
.Va agent_binary .
.It Va agent_ref
The branch or tag to build.
Default: the repository's own.
.It Va android
A block naming an Android app that may log in:
.Va package ,
its package name, and
.Va fingerprints ,
the SHA-256 fingerprints of the certificates it is signed with, as
Android's
.Cm apksigner
or
.Cm keytool
print them, with or without colons; at most 8.
The console then serves
.Pa /.well-known/assetlinks.json
naming the app, which Android asks for before it lets the app use the
keys registered for
.Va rp_id ,
and takes WebAuthn ceremonies made in the app, whose origin is
.Ql android:apk-key-hash:\&
and the base64url of one of the fingerprints, as well as those of
.Va origin .
.Va rp_id
must be the host name the console is reached by for Android to find
the file.
Without the block,
.Pa /.well-known/assetlinks.json
is not found and only
.Va origin
is taken.
.It Ic cluster Brq Va self Va listen Va nodes
Consoles that are one, active on every node: each serves its browsers
and reads its own copy of the data directory's documents, and every
change is the cluster's.
The nodes elect a leader (Raft) over the arcana-cluster family on
.Va listen ,
a cblink URI
.Pq Li tcp://[::]:4311 ;
the leader numbers each change and answers once a majority of the
nodes holds it, and every node writes it in turn.
.Va nodes
names each node with its
.Va uri
and its
.Va origin ;
.Va self
is this one's name.
The first node named is the seed: its documents are the cluster's when
it starts, sent whole to a node that has none; the others' are replaced.
Three nodes, or five, keep a majority when one, or two, stop; a node
cut off from the majority reads, and refuses changes.
The workflow scheduler, the SD-WAN manager and mail run on the leader
alone.
Each node needs the CA of the first:
.Pa ca.pem
and
.Pa ca.key
copied to its
.Va datadir
before it starts; it makes its own certificate of that CA,
.Pa cluster/node.pem ,
which says
.Li urn:arcana:role:console
and its host's name, and the nodes take each other by it.
.Va rp_id
is a name every node's origin is under
.Pq Li console.example No for Li https://a.console.example ,
so that a security key registered on one signs in on every one.
.El
.Pp
The settings
.Va rp_name ,
.Va update_check ,
.Va update_url ,
.Va agent_binary ,
.Va agent_source
and
.Va agent_ref
can also be changed from the console, under Settings.
What is set there is kept in
.Pa settings.json
in
.Va datadir
and overrides
.Pa web.conf ;
a value put back to that of
.Pa web.conf
follows it again.
The others are read once, when the console starts, from
.Pa web.conf
alone.
.Pp
The module checks every certificate it is configured with when it
loads, and refuses to start with the reason in the log; Kore serves
HTTPS only with an RSA certificate.
.Sh FIRST LOGIN
With no security key registered, the console writes a one-time token to
.Pa setup-token
in
.Va datadir
and says so in its log.
The first registration in the browser needs it; later keys are added
from a logged-in session.
A key may be a hardware key or a passkey, such as a phone's.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It Pa /usr/local/etc/arcana/kore.conf
.It Pa /usr/local/etc/arcana/web.conf
.It Pa /usr/local/etc/arcana/routes.conf
The configuration; the first two have samples next to them.
.It Pa /usr/local/lib/arcana/arcana-console.so
The module.
.It Pa /usr/local/www/arcana-console
The web application.
.It Pa /var/db/arcana
.Pa credentials.json ,
.Pa servers.json ,
.Pa setup-token ,
and with the console's own authority
.Pa ca.pem ,
.Pa ca.key ,
.Pa console.pem ,
.Pa console.key .
.It Pa /usr/local/etc/rc.d/arcana
The
.Xr rc 8
script; variables
.Va arcana_console_enable ,
.Va arcana_console_config
and
.Va arcana_console_web_conf .
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr kore 1 ,
.Xr arcana-agent 8 ,
.Xr arcana-enrol 8 ,
.Xr arcanactl 8 ,
.Xr jailconf 8
.Pp
The API is described in
.Pa docs/openapi.yaml
of the source tree.
